{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>קשט</b> — on the pattern of verbs, like <i>ישט</i>." "<b>אמרים אמת</b> — the correct form is אמרי אמת. And likewise טורים אבן סיגים כסף אילים צמר, and so [there are] many on the pattern of the short [construct]." "<b>וטעם להשיב</b> — like 'and Moses returned the words of the people to YHWH' (Exodus 19:8), that is: when I make known to you קשט of words of truth, thus I will return to him words, like 'we will do and we will hear.'" "<b>לשולחיך</b> — to the name [= the one] who sent me to discipline you, for the intellect is the messenger of HaShem. 'לשולחיך' is in the plural, like <i>אלוה עושי</i>."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:15.111016221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}